# Copyright Complaints (DMCA) for {{PRODUCT_NAME}}

**Effective date:** {{EFFECTIVE_DATE}}

{{ENTITY_NAME}} respects copyright. If you think something on {{PRODUCT_NAME}} copies your work without permission, you can ask us to remove it.

## Where to send a notice
**Designated agent:** {{DMCA_AGENT_NAME_OR_ROLE}}
**Email:** {{DMCA_EMAIL}}
**Mailing address:** {{DMCA_ADDRESS}}

## What to include
A valid notice has all of these:
1. Your name and contact details.
2. A description of the copyrighted work you say was copied.
3. Where the material is on {{PRODUCT_NAME}} (a URL is best).
4. A statement that you believe in good faith that the use is not allowed by the owner, their agent, or the law.
5. A statement that the information in your notice is accurate and, under penalty of perjury, that you are the owner or authorized to act for the owner.
6. Your physical or electronic signature.

Notices that leave out these items may not be acted on. Knowingly false notices can lead to liability.

## What we do
We review notices and, when they look complete, we remove or disable access to the material and tell the person who posted it. {{DMCA_PROCESS_DETAILS}}

## Counter-notice
If you posted the material and think it was removed by mistake, you can send a counter-notice to the same address with:
1. Your name, contact details, and signature.
2. What was removed and where it was before removal.
3. A statement, under penalty of perjury, that you believe in good faith it was removed by mistake or misidentification.
4. Your consent to the court in your district (or, if outside the US, any district where we can be found) and that you will accept service from the person who sent the notice.

If we get a valid counter-notice we pass it to the complainant and may restore the material in {{COUNTER_NOTICE_WAIT_PERIOD}} unless they tell us they have started a court action.

